---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PromptBlock from '../../components/PromptBlock.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Productivity cookbook · Pace"
  description="Productivity recipes for the Pace marketplace. Cross-app task management. End-of-day update that pulls from everywhere. Project memory that survives context switches."
  activeNav="cookbook"
  canonicalPath="/cookbook/productivity"
>
  <article class="usecases-page">
    <header class="usecases-team-page-head">
      <a class="usecases-back-link" href="/cookbook">&larr; All cookbooks</a>
      <span class="usecases-eyebrow">Productivity cookbook</span>
      <h1>Productivity</h1>
      <p class="usecases-team-page-tagline">The cross-role utility belt: managers writing status updates, ICs assembling end-of-day recaps, founders searching for the decision they made three sprints ago. Install regardless of role; pair with whichever team plugin you already use.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="usecases-team-page-body">
<article class="usecase-card usecase-card-marquee">
        <span class="usecase-card-badge">Marquee recipe</span>
        <h3>Daily update that pulls itself together</h3>
        <p class="usecase-outcome">Async standups stop being a chore.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, schedule, weekdays 17:30</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>update</code>, <code>task-management</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (cloud schedule), Slack + Notion + Linear connectors, plan mode</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>End of the day, the routine assembles what you shipped (commits, tickets closed, Slack threads contributed to) and drafts a one-paragraph wrap; rolls open work into tomorrow's queue. Plan mode parks the draft for your edit before it posts to your team's standup channel. Async standups stop being a chore.</p>

        <div class="usecase-setup">
          <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>
          <ol class="usecase-steps">
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Install the productivity plugin</h5>
                <div class="usecase-step-actions">
                  <a class="usecase-step-btn" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=productivity" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Install in Cowork &nearr;</a>
                  <code class="usecase-step-cmd">claude plugin install productivity@pace</code>
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Authorize Slack, Linear, Notion, and GitHub</h5>
                <p>Whatever subset you use. The skill pulls signals from each, so the more sources connected the richer the wrap.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Create the scheduled routine</h5>
                <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Routines</strong> &rarr; <strong>New routine</strong> &rarr; <strong>Schedule</strong> &middot; <strong>Weekdays</strong> &middot; <strong>17:30</strong>.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">4</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>
                <p>Edit the channel + role-focus line to match your team.</p>
                <PromptBlock prompt={`End of day check-in. Run update to assemble
what I shipped today: commits merged, Linear tickets I
moved, Slack threads I contributed substantively to, docs
I edited in Notion.

Then run task-management to roll my open
items into tomorrow's queue (carry forward unchecked
todos, surface things I said I'd do but haven't).

Draft a 3-line async standup post in our voice:
"Yesterday I... Today I will... Blockers: ..."

Use plan mode : show me the draft for a quick edit
before posting to #async-standup.`} />
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="usecase-step">
              <span class="usecase-step-num">5</span>
              <div class="usecase-step-body">
                <h5>Click <strong>Run now</strong> to verify</h5>
                <p>The first run today shows you the draft format. Plan mode means you approve before it posts. Tomorrow at 17:30 it runs again automatically : you'll get a notification in the Claude app when the draft is ready for your edit.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Project memory that follows you across sessions</h3>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Interactive, when starting work after a break</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>memory-management</code>, <code>start</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Auto memory (CLAUDE.md), cross-app context retrieval</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p><code>start</code> re-hydrates yesterday's context from <code>memory-management</code>: open threads, the decisions you made, the things you said you'd come back to. No more spending the first 20 minutes of every session reading old messages.</p>
              <div class="usecase-setup">

                <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to use it</h4>

                <ol class="usecase-steps">

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Ready to use</h5>

                      <p>No routine to configure for this one. Just open Cowork (or Claude Code) and paste the prompt below.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Try it with this prompt</h5>

                      <PromptBlock prompt={`I need to find: [what we decided about pricing in the Q3 launch retro].

Search across Slack channel histories (#product, #pricing, #leadership), Notion docs, Linear comments, and GitHub PR discussion. Surface the actual decision (not just the discussion), with the date it was made and a link back to the source.`} label="Project memory prompt" />

                    </div>

                  </li>

                </ol>

              </div>
      </article>
      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>End-of-week recap, written for you</h3>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Routine, schedule, weekly Friday 17:00</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>update</code>, <code>tasks</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Routines (cloud schedule), Linear + GitHub + calendar connectors, multi-source pull</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p>Pulls what you shipped, what you reviewed, what you started, and what slipped. Drafts the recap email or status update in your voice, ready to send (or skip) on Monday. Trains itself on your past updates after a few weeks so the tone matches.</p>
              <PromptBlock prompt={`Every Friday at 5pm, pull what I shipped this week (Linear closed, GitHub merged), what I reviewed (PRs I commented on), what I started (branches created), and what slipped (carryover from last week's plan).

Draft my recap email in my voice, ready to send Monday morning. Match the tone of recent recaps I've sent (read the last three from my sent folder).

Park the draft in Notion under /personal/recaps so I can edit before sending.`} label="Weekly recap prompt" />
      </article>

      <article class="usecase-card">
        <h3>Project memory: search across every decision your team made</h3>
        <p>Ask "what did we decide about pricing in the Q3 launch retro?" and Claude searches across Slack, Notion, Linear comments, and GitHub PR threads simultaneously, surfaces the actual decision (not just the discussion), and links back to source. The work of remembering moves from you to the agent.</p>
        <dl class="usecase-meta">
          <div><dt>Trigger</dt><dd>Cowork chat, on demand</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Skills</dt><dd><code>memory-search</code>, <code>synthesize</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>Cowork chat, multi-source connectors (Slack + Notion + Linear + GitHub), enterprise-search pairing</dd></div>
        </dl>
              <div class="usecase-setup">

                <h4 class="usecase-setup-title">How to set it up</h4>

                <ol class="usecase-steps">

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">1</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Create the Cowork hook</h5>

                      <p>In Cowork, open <strong>Hooks</strong> &rarr; <strong>New hook</strong>. Match the trigger described above (file upload, message, schedule).</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">2</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Paste this as the routine prompt</h5>

                      <PromptBlock prompt={`I need to find: [what we decided about pricing in the Q3 launch retro].

Search across Slack channel histories (#product, #pricing, #leadership), Notion docs, Linear comments, and GitHub PR discussion. Surface the actual decision (not just the discussion), with the date it was made and a link back to the source.`} label="Project memory prompt" />

                    </div>

                  </li>

                  <li class="usecase-step">

                    <span class="usecase-step-num">3</span>

                    <div class="usecase-step-body">

                      <h5>Click <strong>Run now</strong> to verify</h5>

                      <p>Eyeball the first run for accuracy. Once it looks right, the routine fires on its trigger from then on. Assumes the plugin from the marquee above is already installed and connectors authorized.</p>

                    </div>

                  </li>

                </ol>

              </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <footer class="usecases-footer">
      <p>
        Have a productivity workflow that should live here? <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/Pace/issues/new">Open an issue</a> with the trigger, skills, and Claude features it uses; we'll fold it into the cookbook.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .usecases-page {
    max-width: var(--width-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-3xl);
  }
  .usecases-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .usecases-lede strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  /* Engineering callout above the TOC */
  .usecases-eng-callout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.78;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-eyebrow::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.4vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-text p {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-radius: 2px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out-quart);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .usecases-eng-callout-cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecases-eng-callout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: var(--spacing-md);
    }
  }

  /* TOC grid */
  .usecases-toc {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  .usecases-toc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    display: block;
    margin: 0 6px var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart),
                transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .usecases-toc-grid a:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    transform: translateY(-1px);
  }
  .usecases-toc-name {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-toc-count {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-ash);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .usecases-toc-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .usecases-team {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .usecases-team-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecases-team-head h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-team-tagline {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card {
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecase-card-marquee {
    border-color: var(--color-forest);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-paper-elev) 92%, var(--color-forest-dim));
  }
  .usecase-card-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecase-card-badge::before {
    content: "";
    display: inline-block;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: currentColor;
  }
  .usecase-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .usecase-card > p {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);
  }
  /* Meta: small chip row at the bottom (was a big dl block at top) */
  .usecase-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 8px;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta > div {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .usecase-meta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .usecase-meta dt::after {
    content: ":";
    margin-left: 1px;
    color: var(--color-mist);
  }
  .usecase-meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: 11px;
  }
  .usecase-meta dd code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }
  .usecase-card p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecase-card p code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-footer {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .usecases-footer a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch a,
  .usecases-impeccable-when a,
  .usecases-team-tagline a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-pitch code,
  .usecases-impeccable-when code,
  .usecases-team-tagline code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-cta .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart), color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .cta-primary {
    background: var(--color-forest);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }
  .cta-primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-hover);
  }
  .cta-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .cta-secondary:hover {
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when summary::before {
    content: '+';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-right: var(--spacing-sm);
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when[open] summary::before {
    content: '−';
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when p,
  .usecases-impeccable-when ul {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .usecases-impeccable-when strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .usecase-meta > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2px;
    }
  }

  /* Recipe card outcome-first ordering: prose before pills */
  .usecase-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .usecase-card h3 { order: 1; }
  .usecase-card-badge { order: 0; }
  .usecase-card > p { order: 2; }
  .usecase-card .usecase-meta { order: 3; margin-top: var(--spacing-md); }


  /* Outcome line at the top of every marquee card. Big bold one-liner
     that tells the visitor what they actually get before the prose. */
  .usecase-outcome {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
    font-weight: 500;
